A Trie node typically contains:
1.  An array or hash map of child pointers (e.g., `children[26]` for lowercase English letters, or `Map<Character, TrieNode>`). Each entry points to a child node representing the next character in a prefix.
2.  A boolean flag (e.g., `isEndOfWord`) indicating whether the path to this node from the root forms a complete word.
```java
class TrieNode {
    Map<Character, TrieNode> children;
    boolean isEndOfWord;

    public TrieNode() {
        children = new HashMap<>();
        isEndOfWord = false;
    }
}
```
